# ask.py start=2026-11-23T18:40:15-05:00 38400 8N1
help home
home    ;; home all axes
home <axis #> [<axis #> ...] 

  Homes one or more axes. If no axis is specified then all robot
axes, including the a track if any, are homed.

$ help calseek
/diag/calseek <axis #>


$ help cal
/diag/cal    ;; calibrate all robot axes
/diag/cal <axis #> [<axis #> ...]

  Calibrates one, more than one, or all axes. WARNING - this will
overwrite the existing calibration file (/conf/robot.cal).

$ help srvstat
/diag/srvstat

 Displays low level information axis servo information. 

$ help zero
/diag/zero

  Zeros the position registers of all robot axes.
WARNING: this command is generally used in preparation for
calibrating the robot and is not used in normal operations.

$ help xzero
/diag/xzero <axis #>

  Zeros the position registers of a particular robot axis.
WARNING: this command is generally used in preparation for 
calibrating the robot and is not used in normal operations.

$ help calrdy
calrdy

  Moves the robot the calibration ready position.

$ 